  <h2>Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Check the forecasts.</b> The University of South Florida publishes a monthly Atlantic sargassum outlook, and Quintana Roo (Mexico) runs a daily colour-coded beach map.</li>
    <li><b>Ask your hotel</b> whether it clears the beach daily — many big resorts do, and some install barriers.</li>
    <li><b>Book flexibly</b> for May to August, or pick a resort with a pool you’ll be happy to use instead.</li>
    <li><b>Don’t swim in thick mats</b> of seaweed, and avoid sitting for long next to large rotting piles.</li>
  </ul>
